.TH MUIDEMO 1
.SH NAME
muidemo \- the toolkit, in a window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B muidemo
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Muidemo
opens a window on the draw server and lays out a panel built from
.IR mui (2):
a title, a row of three buttons, a checkmark and a label, a text
field with its own label, and a row of
.B OK
and
.B Quit
buttons.
It runs the toolkit's own event loop and draws nothing itself; the
object tree says what the window holds, and the theme (see
.IR theme (6))
says what it looks like.
The window is titled
.BR Workbench ,
though this program is a demonstration, not the desktop shell.
.PP
A click on a button, or the keyboard reaching the focused one, reaches
a handler in the program.
.B Quit
and
.B OK
both close the window and end the program.
Every other button and the checkmark are for show and do nothing else.
.SH SOURCE
.B apps/muidemo/main.odin
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR window (1),
.IR mui (2),
.IR theme (6)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The exit status is empty, or
.B open
if the window could not be opened.
.SH BUGS
Nothing in the panel is wired to a real action; every gadget but
.B OK
and
.B Quit
is decorative.
